          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గడ్డం — gaḍḍaṁ — \"the chin; a beard\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గడ్డం (gaḍḍaṁ) is native Dravidian, one word with Kannada gaḍḍa, \"the beard about the chin, the chin\" (DEDR 1156). DEDR notes that Tamil keṭṭam, \"beard\", is a loan from Telugu, and compares Prakrit khaḍḍa, \"beard\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
